{
 "schema": "eqbench-measurement-subset-v1",
 "purpose": "Fixed measurement subset used to compare checker behaviour before/after a change (see README 'Measurement subset'). Run it with eqbench_run_subset.sh, then compare the two result trees with reporting.outcome_transition and check them with reporting.soundness_gate.",
 "ground_truth_note": "This manifest is NOT an oracle. The only ground truth is the benchmark label: sample_identity containing '/Eq/' means the pair must never be NOT_EQ, and '/Neq/' means it must never be EQUIVALENT. 'observed_baseline' merely records what the checker produced at the commit named below and may itself be wrong (an EQUIVALENT can be an accidental result of an implementation defect). Do not treat observed_baseline as expected output; use it only to explain transitions.",
 "selection_criteria": [
  "Eq: single-function sources only (one source == one function == 8 pairs); per benchmark family at most one source whose selected pairs were 'mixed' (EQUIVALENT+UNKNOWN) or all-UNKNOWN in the full baseline, plus REVE/barthe2big as the TIMEOUT-containing source. Families whose cheapest source exceeded the time budget (bess, gam, tsafe) are not represented.",
  "Neq: single-function sources only, one per benchmark family preferring sources with at least one NOT_EQ, plus raytrace/sphere and raytrace/surface (known EQUIVALENT-in-Neq and ERROR cases used to exercise the soundness gate) and optimization/wood (TIMEOUT pairs).",
  "Pair ids cover arm64/mips64 x clang/gcc, same-compiler optimisation steps (B1_B2, B5_B7, B9_B10, B13_B15) and cross-ISA / cross-compiler pairs (B1_B9, B6_B14, B3_B11, B4_B16); Neq ids are the corresponding N_/O_ same-ISA pairs.",
  "Budget: the production runners keep only one function (8 pairs) in flight at a time, so wall time is the sum of per-function maxima plus ~17 s runner overhead per function. Each half is sized to stay under ~9 minutes and eqbench_run_subset.sh runs the two halves concurrently (8 + 8 slots <= PARALLEL_JOBS=20) so the whole subset finishes within 10 minutes."
 ],
 "run_settings": {
  "PARALLEL_JOBS": 20,
  "EQBENCH_RESOURCE_ADMISSION": 0,
  "EQBENCH_BUILD_POLICY": "PREBUILT_ONLY",
  "PAIR_PROCESS_TIMEOUT": "240s",
  "note": "Full runs use PAIR_PROCESS_TIMEOUT=600s. The subset uses 240s so that TIMEOUT-prone pairs stay inside the 10 minute budget; a pair reported as TIMEOUT by the subset is therefore not directly comparable with the full-run outcome of the same pair."
 },
